{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Rabbi Moses said: the sense is 'vindicate me, according to my righteousness, against those who oppress me.' But the correct view in my eyes is: 'For You, HaShem, judge the earth; <b>vindicate me</b> according to <b>my righteousness</b>, for I have not repaid Cush with evil.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:30.021030085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}